# The event log is append-only, and a merge of two append-only files is the
# concatenation of both. `union` is one of git's built-in low-level merge
# drivers, so this needs no configuration on anyone's machine.
#
# Sharding one file per actor already removes almost all contention: two agents
# with different names never touch the same file. This covers the remainder --
# the same actor emitting from two worktrees, or a shard modified on both a
# tranche branch and develop -- where the correct resolution is always "keep
# both lines" and asking a human to hand-merge JSONL would be a good way to
# lose an event.
#
# Losing a line here is not like losing a line in source: a dropped event is a
# finding that silently never happened, and nothing downstream can notice.
*.jsonl merge=union
